@@ -1338,6 +1338,16 @@ By default, column types are automatically detected for CSV or TSV files - resul
 
 Detected types are only applied when the table is created by the command. Inserting CSV or TSV data into a table that already exists leaves the existing column types unchanged - values are inserted using the table's existing schema.
 
+You can explicitly set a column type using ``--type COLUMN TYPE``. This option can be repeated, and the supported types are ``text``, ``integer``, ``float`` and ``blob``:
+
+.. code-block:: bash
+
+    sqlite-utils insert creatures.db creatures creatures.csv --csv \
+        --type age integer \
+        --type weight float
+
+Explicit types take precedence over automatically detected types. Unlike detected types, explicit types are also applied to tables that already exist. The same option is available on ``sqlite-utils upsert``.
+
 For example, given a ``creatures.csv`` file containing this:
 
